    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2T8E7LhF3ZQzmWj4pm3aP7Z)_\n\nReplaces #227, closed because its branch name did not match its number.\n\n## Summary\nOne doc, `docs/tangles/funct/sp-org-lint.org`, now tangles the whole `sp-org-lint` family into separate `.el` files:\n\n- `sp-org-lint.el`: only `require`s for the submodules below.\n- `sp-org-lint-others.el`: everything not in a bigger submodule (the list commands).\n- `sp-org-lint-footnotes.el`: the footnote linter and its headless worker (the worker now loads only this file).\n- `sp-author-notes.el`, `sp-author-notes-bibtex.el`, `sp-litnotes-refs.el`, `sp-litnotes-titles.el`: unchanged code, docs moved here from their own docs and from `sp-academic.org`.\n\nThe table of contents at the top of `sp-academic.org` lists the four author and litnote lint modules (marked \"Author lint\" / \"Litnote lint\") with links to the new sections and the commands named. README, CHANGELOG and `.el` docstrings point to the new place. `sp-split-leave-parents` is documented here as before but not required by `sp-org-lint`.\n\n## Test plan\n- [x] `tools/check-tangle.sh` in Emacs 29.3.\n- [x] ERT: author-notes 18, author-notes-bibtex 4, litnotes-refs 6, litnotes-titles 8 pass. `sp-org-lint-test` passes except `sp-org-lint-footnote-async-scan-and-apply`, which also fails on main (the worker's `emacs -Q` has no `sp-var-dir`).\n- [ ] CI tangle check; open `sp-org-lint.org` in Emacs; run `M-x sp-org-lint-footnotes` and `sp-org-lint-list` in the real config.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01WWLNiBdNucJCEhP3kY1oNm)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01WWLNiBdNucJCEhP3kY1oNm",
